            "title": "Removal of BOM and EOL escaping breaks expected behavior",
            "severity": "high",
            "file": "lib/box/file.js",
            "line": 23,
            "explanation": "The change removes escapeBOM and escapeEOL utilities and the option to escape BOM and Windows line endings on reading file content. The previous code defaulted to escape=true in wrapReadOptions and applied escapeContent in read and readSync methods. Removing this causes files containing BOM or Windows EOL to no longer be escaped, breaking existing usage and tests that expect this behavior.",
            "suggestion": "Restore escapeBOM and escapeEOL imports and usage. Keep the 'escape' option defaulting to true in wrapReadOptions. Apply escapeContent when reading file content if escape option is true, both in async read and readSync methods.",
            "failureAfterChange": "Reading a file with UTF-8 BOM will return the BOM character included instead of stripped. For example, reading a content buffer '\\ufefffoo' will yield the string with BOM '\\ufefffoo' instead of 'foo'.",
